   54|       |    /** The binary representation of (p + 1)/4 has 3 blocks of 1s, with lengths in
   55|       |     *  { 2, 22, 223 }. Use an addition chain to calculate 2^n - 1 for each block:
   56|       |     *  1, [2], 3, 6, 9, 11, [22], 44, 88, 176, 220, [223]
